Online shop built in PHP with a custom router, product catalog, shopping cart, authentication, checkout flow, freight rules, and Prisjakt XML export. The project includes a MySQL database schema and seed data for demo products and shipping zones.

Features
Product listing with category filtering
Product detail page
Shopping cart with add/remove functionality
User registration and login
Order checkout flow
Freight calculation based on shipping zones
Database-driven product and category data
Prisjakt product feed export in XML format
MySQL schema and seed data included
Tech Stack
PHP
MySQL
PDO
Composer
Custom routing
XML generation for Prisjakt feed
Project Structure
api/ — API endpoints and XML feed
assets/ — images and static assets
components/ — reusable UI components
config/ — database and app configuration
DB/ — database schema and seed files
Models/ — domain models
pages/ — page controllers/views
repositories/ — database access logic
utils/ — helper classes and router
css/ — styling
js/ — frontend scripts
Requirements
Before running the project, make sure you have:

PHP 8+
MySQL or MariaDB
Composer
A local web server or PHP built-in server
Database Setup
Create a MySQL database.

Import the schema file:
mysql -u root -p your_database < schema.sql

Import the seed data:
mysql -u root -p your_database < seed.sql

Environment Configuration
Create a .env file in the project root and add the following values:

DATABASE_HOST=localhost
DATABASE_NAME=book_shop
DATABASE_USER=root
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your_password
DATABASE_PORT=3306

Do not commit real credentials to GitHub. Use local values only or add a .env.example if needed.

Run the Project
From the project root, start the PHP development server:

php -S localhost:8000 index.php

Then open:

http://localhost:8000

Prisjakt Feed
The project includes a feed at:

http://localhost:8000/prisjakt.xml

This export generates XML for product listings and supports product image metadata.

Notes
This project is designed as a learning project and uses custom PHP routing instead of a framework. The database schema and seed data are included for easy setup and testing.